[{:adr/consequences "{:no_single_finish_commit \"this is a long-running multi-increment effort, same as genko's\\n                            already-real 2-increments-in-progress state; this ADR's\\n                            concrete output is the full research ground truth, the first\\n                            landed increment, and a sequencing plan -- not a finished port\", :consumers_unaffected \"no immediate breaking change forced on any of the 7 real consumer\\n                         apps\", :subtleties_to_preserve_not_silently_fix [\"BoneController.setBone's single-axis-quaternion overwrite (clobbers other axes\\n     previously set on the same bone)\" \"createConversationController.idleMicro's same-class Z-only quaternion clobber\" \"createMotionPlayer's Rust-WASM branch is dead in practice (kami param never passed at\\n     the one real createVrmEngine call site) -- the TS evaluateTS switch is what's actually\\n     exercised\" \"createVoiceSynth.speak()'s speaking flag not reset on the Kokoro no-audio success path\\n     (only playAudio's onended/catch and explicit stop() reset it)\" \"NodeRow.svelte's collapse-arrow glyph is hardcoded to always ▼, never ▶, even when\\n     collapsed (the collapsed $derived value is computed but unused)\" \"Toolbar.svelte's paper-texture selector is local-state-only and functionally inert (no\\n     onpaperchange prop exists)\" \"FloatingTools' onundo/onredo props are wired to console.info stubs in Genko.svelte\\n     instead of that file's own real undo()/redo() functions\"]}", :adr/authoritative_for ["kami-engine-sdk (kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk, Svelte 5, 11 modules ~91 files) is being\n    migrated to ClojureScript INCREMENTALLY -- one function/component at a time, each\n    delegated to a cljc SSoT and verified before the next -- NOT as a big-bang rewrite;\n    this follows the already-in-flight ADR-2607020200 genko precedent (2 real increments\n    landed 2026-07-02) discovered mid-task, which explicitly overrode an initial\n    full-rewrite scoping" "call/webvr's protocol layer (turn.ts HMAC-SHA1 credentials, wire.ts CBOR signaling)\n    delegates to ALREADY-EXISTING cljc SSoT repos kotoba-lang/turn|rt|net|signal (CLJC\n    reimplementations of the Rust kotoba-turn/kotoba-rt/kotoba-net/kotoba-signal crates\n    removed by kotoba-lang/kotoba PR #259) -- not new repos to create" "first real increment landed this ADR: kotoba-lang/turn commit 2d90bddc added\n    mint-credential-scoped/verify-credential-scoped to kotoba.turn.credential, matching\n    turn.ts's exact room/player-scoped username encoding and reason-reporting verify\n    result shape, with JVM tests replicating all 7 of turn.test.ts's assertions -- turn.ts\n    itself does NOT yet delegate to this (that needs a shadow-cljs globalThis.KotobaTurn\n    bridge, mirroring kami-genko's :genko build, not yet built)" "consumer apps (cyber-drill, ai-gftd-mangaka, image2metahuman, image2vrm,\n    etzhayyim-project-baminiku, sumitsubo, kotodama-host-sdk) are explicitly OUT OF SCOPE\n    for this migration -- they keep using the current published Svelte package at their\n    pinned version until they separately choose to migrate" "kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk-clj is confirmed NOT the SSoT target for builders/\n    components -- its own README states it's an unrelated project (scene/ECS/render-IR/WIT\n    contract authoring, not UI-component/controller logic)"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kami-engine-sdk-svelte-retirement", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607020200-mangaka-genko-cljc.md"], :adr/status "proposed", :adr/id "adr-2607052000-kami-engine-sdk-svelte-retirement-cljs-migration", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-05", :adr/decision "{:methodology {:what \"migrate module-by-module: pure logic -> cljc SSoT (existing repo if one already\\n          canonically owns that logic, new repo split out only if none does) -> compiled\\n          globalThis.<Name> JS bridge -> TS/Svelte host delegates one function/component at\\n          a time -> verify (browser if a live host exists, JVM/nbb test if not) -> next\\n          increment. Exactly ADR-2607020200's genko shape, generalized to the other 10\\n          modules.\", :process_constraints [\"no wholesale rewrite commits -- one function/component/small cohesive group per\\n     commit, never a whole module at once\" \"delegate to an existing canonical SSoT before creating a new one (turn/rt/net/signal,\\n     kami-genko) -- do not build a second competing implementation of the same protocol\" \"verify before moving to the next increment -- real browser when a live host exists\\n     (genko's own precedent), JVM/nbb test otherwise\" \"host/DOM/WASM stays host; only pure logic moves to cljc -- same split\\n     ADR-2607020200 already established for genko's oplog/tree/doc-model vs its\\n     WebGPU/DOM runtime\"]}, :per_module_plan {:call_webvr {:turn_ts {:ssot \"kotoba-lang/turn (kotoba.turn.credential)\", :status \"first increment LANDED: mint-credential-scoped/\\n                       verify-credential-scoped added, commit 2d90bddc, JVM tests replicate\\n                       all 7 turn.test.ts assertions\", :not_yet_done \"wiring turn.ts itself to delegate to a compiled\\n                             globalThis.KotobaTurn.* bridge -- needs a new shadow-cljs.edn\\n                             :browser build + install! init-fn in kotoba-lang/turn (mirror\\n                             of kami-genko's :genko build target), not built yet\"}, :wire_ts {:ssot \"kotoba-lang/rt or kotoba-lang/signal (whichever owns the kotoba-rt\\n                     CBOR wire-format port)\", :status \"not started\"}, :call_ts {:note \"RTCPeerConnection/WebSocket orchestration is inherently host/browser-\\n                     API code, not pure logic -- likely stays a thin host shell calling\\n                     into the wire/turn cljc bridges, matching genko's host/cljc split\", :status \"not started\"}, :webvr_incident_pregel {:note \"applySelection/initialState (the actually-executed pure state machine --\\n            INCIDENT_GRAPH's compiled StateGraph is vestigial/unused at runtime) is a\\n            good small next candidate: pure, fully tested, no host/DOM coupling\", :ssot \"not yet chosen -- candidate: new small kami-webvr-clj, or fold into\\n            kotoba-lang/rt if scope allows; decide at that increment's start\", :status \"not started\"}}, :genko {:note \"already in progress under ADR-2607020200/kotoba-lang/kami-genko --\\n                  continue its existing 移植#N numbering, do not restart or duplicate\", :flagged_bug \"Genko.svelte's FloatingTools onundo/onredo callbacks are wired to\\n                         console.info stubs instead of the component's own real undo()/\\n                         redo() functions -- worth fixing in a future genko increment, not\\n                         this ADR's concern directly\"}, :builders_components {:ssot \"new cljc SSoT, name TBD at that increment's start -- NOT\\n           kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk-clj (confirmed different/unrelated project per its\\n           own README); likely a new kami-vrm-controllers-clj split from kami-engine's\\n           monorepo, same pattern as kami-mangaka-genko-clj -> kami-genko\", :good_first_candidates [\"data/joint-limits.ts's clampBoneDeg/clampBoneRad -- pure, already has a documented\\n      Rust counterpart (kami-skeleton::defaultHumanoidConstraints)\" \"data/emotion-patterns.ts's analyzeTextEmotion/emotionToMorphWeights -- pure\\n      regex+arithmetic, well-isolated\"], :do_last \"VrmViewer/VrmCanvas/panel components -- highest-risk, ~1370 lines of\\n              imperative WebGPU/WebGL/DOM in Canvas.svelte alone; ports mechanically once\\n              the pure logic underneath is already cljc\", :status \"not started\"}, :small_utility_modules {:modules [\"gsplat\" \"manufacturing\" \"document\" \"trackpad\"], :note \"all four are already plain framework-agnostic TypeScript (zero Svelte runes),\\n           each with real test coverage -- lowest-risk, most mechanical ports in the whole\\n           SDK, good early increments since they carry no UI-reactivity-mapping risk\", :ssot \"likely a new kami-industrial-clj-family split; decide per-module at increment\\n           time\", :status \"not started\"}}, :consumer_migration {:in_scope false, :note \"cyber-drill, ai-gftd-mangaka, image2metahuman, image2vrm,\\n          etzhayyim-project-baminiku, sumitsubo, kotodama-host-sdk are unaffected until\\n          they explicitly upgrade -- the published Svelte package keeps working at its\\n          current pinned version throughout\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"user direction 2026-07-05: '@etzhayyim/kami-engine-sdk を svelte から cljs に\\n           して. svelte は退役' -- convert kami-engine-sdk from Svelte to ClojureScript,\\n           Svelte is being retired org-wide\", :investigated [\"kami-engine-sdk full inventory: 11 modules (~91 files) -- builders (9, headless Svelte-5\\n    -runes controllers wrapping KamiWasmExports), components (13, VrmViewer/VrmCanvas/\\n    IsekaiCanvas/panels/CallPanel Svelte components), call (8, plain TS WebRTC signaling +\\n    TURN credentials + CBOR wire codec, zero Svelte), webvr (7, mostly plain TS choice-\\n    scenario state machine + one Svelte-runes engine file), genko (21, manga editor --\\n    components/stores/canvas-pregel), gsplat/manufacturing/trackpad/document (11 total,\\n    all plain TS), data/types (20, pure preset/type data). 5 parallel deep-read agents\\n    produced complete, literal, file-by-file ground truth for every module (retained in\\n    session transcript).\" \"real consumers confirmed via grep across orgs/: ai-gftd-cyber-drill, ai-gftd-mangaka,\\n    etzhayyim-project-image2metahuman, etzhayyim-project-image2vrm,\\n    etzhayyim-project-baminiku, sumitsubo/sdk, kotoba-kotodama/kotodama-host-sdk -- all\\n    import the Svelte package via package.json; user confirmed these are follow-up, not\\n    this migration's scope\" \"CRITICAL discovery mid-task: 90-docs/adr/2607020200-mangaka-genko-cljc.md documents an\\n    already-real, in-flight incremental migration for the genko module specifically -- 2\\n    increments (移植#1/#2, commits 67c3ce5/517bd8d, 2026-07-02, user-authored) already\\n    landed, each delegating ONE pure function (allNodes, wouldCycle) from genko-embed.ts's\\n    inline JS to globalThis.KamiGenko (a compiled kotoba-lang/kami-genko cljc SSoT bundle),\\n    each verified in a real browser (WebGPU Chrome) before landing. ADR-2607020200's own\\n    text: the TS runtime is NOT replaced wholesale, cljc is a parallel SSoT with a\\n    follow-up to compile+swap incrementally.\" \"second discovery: kotoba-lang/turn, rt, net, signal already exist in manifest/repos.edn\\n    :extra-projects -- CLJC reimplementations of the Rust kotoba-turn/kotoba-rt/kotoba-net/\\n    kotoba-signal crates (removed by kotoba-lang/kotoba PR #259, restored per that repo's\\n    own comment). kami-engine-sdk's turn.ts (HMAC-SHA1 TURN credential mint/verify) and\\n    wire.ts (hand-rolled CBOR signaling codec, byte-compatible with kotoba-rt's Rust\\n    ciborium implementation) are TypeScript reimplementations of exactly what these repos\\n    are the canonical home for -- not new-SSoT-needed territory like genko was.\" \"kotoba-lang/turn's kotoba.turn.credential ns already has hmac-sha1-base64,\\n    constant-time-eq, RFC-2202-tested mint-credential/verify-credential -- but under a\\n    single-opaque-user, plain-boolean-verify contract, not turn.ts's room/player-scoped,\\n    reason-reporting one\"], :risk \"this is a real, published SDK with real external consumers; a wholesale rewrite\\n         risks both duplicating genko's already-in-flight work and introducing regressions\\n         with no verification path for ~40+ Svelte components in one pass. Incremental,\\n         delegate-to-existing-SSoT, verify-each-step is the only responsible path at this\\n         scale.\"}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"full rewrite of all 91 files in one pass, as initially scoped before the\\n            ADR-2607020200 precedent was found\", :rejected_because \"contradicts the user's own established, working, browser-verified\\n                       incremental methodology once discovered; risks duplicating/\\n                       conflicting with genko's already-in-flight increments and\\n                       reinventing what kotoba-lang/turn/rt/net/signal already canonically\\n                       own\"} {:option \"reuse kotoba-lang/kami-engine-sdk-clj for the builders/components port\", :rejected_because \"that repo's own README states it is a different project (scene/ECS/\\n                       render-IR/WIT contract authoring for kami-engine, not a UI-\\n                       component/controller SSoT) -- forcing VRM controller logic into it\\n                       would misuse its documented scope\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607052000: kami-engine-sdk -- retire Svelte, migrate to ClojureScript\n          incrementally (cljc SSoT delegation, per ADR-2607020200's genko precedent)"}]